    <desc>In 1999, the Indian Air Force fought the world's highest aerial battle. 25 years later, we explore the meticulous planning and technical efforts behind it, modifying aircraft with countermeasure systems. Through logbooks, war diaries, footage, and veteran interviews, it was revealed how the IAF's efforts were pivotal in reclaiming crucial high-altitude posts that were intruded by Pakistan</desc>
